# -*- encoding: utf-8 -*-
# Arc: Training | Scene: ChoosingAMentor

translate es strings:

    old "Sarah returned to her tent."
    new "Sarah regresó a su tienda."

    old "Other then her, it was empty. Right now, she welcomed the solitude."
    new "Aparte de ella, todo estaba vacío. En este momento, la soledad le resultaba bienvenida."

    old "She strode across the room and grabbed one of the swords off a nearby crate."
    new "Caminó decidida por la habitación y agarró una de las espadas de una caja cercana."

    old "Sarah felt the weight of the hilt press into her palm."
    new "Sarah sintió el peso del mango presionar su palma."

    old "She had never held a sword in all her life."
    new "Nunca había sostenido una espada en toda su vida."

    old "Back home, in Rosanna, fighting was men's work."
    new "En casa, en Rosanna, la lucha era trabajo de hombres."

    old "No, she thought to herself."
    new "No, pensó para sí misma."

    old "There is no home to go back to. And all the rules that applied were gone."
    new "No hay hogar al que volver. Y todas las reglas que aplicaban, habían desaparecido."

    old "All the world had been tilted upside down."
    new "Todo el mundo había quedado del revés."

    old "She awkwardly tried to raise the sword."
    new "Intentó torpemente levantar la espada."

    old "It was heavier than she had thought."
    new "Era más pesado de lo que había pensado."

    old "Instantly, she knew that she would never stand a chance if she didn't train."
    new "Instantáneamente, supo que nunca tendría oportunidad si no entrenaba."

    old "She had a choice to make."
    new "Tenía que tomar una decisión."

    old "She would need to train for the initiation, but just as Kate had said."
    new "Necesitaría entrenar para la iniciación, pero, tal como Kate había dicho."

    old "she would need a mentor."
    new "necesitaría un mentor."

    old "Someone who could train her, guarantee that she could pass the exam."
    new "Alguien que pudiera entrenarla y garantizar que aprobaría el examen."

    old "In the quiet dark of her new home, Sarah thought about her decision."
    new "En la oscuridad tranquila de su nuevo hogar, Sarah pensó en su decisión."

    old "Decide on a mentor."
    new "Elige a un mentor."

    old "Ask Kate"
    new "Pregúntale a Kate"

    old "Ask Ephraim and Caleb."
    new "Pregúntale a Efraín y a Caleb."

    old "Ask Atilla, the orc."
    new "Pregunta a Attila, el orco."
